    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This book analyzes how the construction and expansion of the United States highway system has transformed urban areas, focusing on the financial costs and economic outcomes of these infrastructure investments.",
      "why": "It provides a detailed, technical evaluation of the historical trade-offs of highway production, challenging the assumption that continued highway expansion yields positive economic returns for American cities."
